  "rationale": "The batch shows severe underweighting for several supported continuations: the empty prefix favors names over the observed opening article, and the sequence This is where our story ends has very low probability for its local continuations. Add an empty-context article rule and suffix-conditioned rules for the observed clause, using ordinary token/POS outputs rather than asserting story phases or target-only semantics. The batch target and replay examples also support a reusable comma-to-proper-name continuation, so add the same comma-conditioned rule to the available proper-name roots rather than conditioning on Lily or Ben individually. These are provisional local generalizations from limited evidence: other openings, words after is/where, and continuations after commas can be valid. The gate must check replay behavior; this patch is not claimed to have passed it.",
